WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.104
What this AI course is: This A I course teaches you to use language models like an engineer, not like magic. You do not need a coding install to start Module 1. Focus on clear goals, constraints, and tests.

2
00:00:13.454 --> 00:00:24.974
What LLMs are good at: Language models are good at drafting, summarising, and transforming text. They follow structured formats when you specify them, and they speed up iteration when you check the output.

3
00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:35.788
What they get wrong: They guess patterns; they do not know truth. They can invent facts, called hallucinations. Vague prompts produce vague, brittle results.

4
00:00:36.138 --> 00:00:49.770
The engineering loop: Use the engineering loop: spec, prompt, evaluate, iterate. Write the goal, inputs, outputs, and failure modes. Keep a small evaluation set and rerun it after every change.

5
00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:59.504
Your Module 1 next step: Open A I Foundations in the course viewer, copy the beginner starter pack templates, and write a one-page summariser spec with ten evaluation cases.
